### Description

I host the model `gpt-5-chat` in Azure and try to connect in our app, but when use stream object that throw this error:

```
[Error [AI_APICallError]: Invalid parameter: 'response_format' of type 'json_schema' is not supported with this model. Learn more about supported models at the Structured Outputs guide: https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/structured-outputs] {
  cause: undefined,
  url: 'https://*****.openai.azure.com/openai/v1/chat/completions?api-version=preview',
  requestBodyValues: [Object],
  statusCode: 400,
  responseHeaders: [Object],
  responseBody: '{\n' +
    '  "error": {\n' +
    `    "message": "Invalid parameter: 'response_format' of type 'json_schema' is not supported with this model. Learn more about supported models at the Structured Outputs guide: https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/structured-outputs",\n` +
    '    "type": "invalid_request_error",\n' +
    '    "param": null,\n' +
    '    "code": null\n' +
    '  }\n' +
    '}',
  isRetryable: false,
  data: [Object]
}
```

Here is the example code:

```ts
const systemPrompt = `You are generating code in ${language}. Produce clean, well-structured code with appropriate comments and error handling.`;
try {
      const { partialObjectStream } = streamObject({
        model,
        system: systemPrompt,
        prompt: title,
        temperature: 0.3,
        schema: z.object({
          code: z.string().describe('The generated code content'),
          language: z
            .enum([
              'javascript',
              'typescript',
              'python',
              'java',
              'csharp',
              'cpp',
              'go',
              'ruby',
              'rust',
              'swift',
              'php',
              'kotlin',
            ])
            .describe('Programming language of the code'),
        }),
      });

      let draftContent = '';

      for await (const element of partialObjectStream) {
        const genCodeContent = {
          code: element.code,
          language: element.language,
        };

        dataStream.write({
          type: 'data-codeDelta',
          data: genCodeContent,
          transient: true,
        });

        draftContent = JSON.stringify(genCodeContent);
      }

      return draftContent;
    } catch (error) {
      logger.error('Error generating gen-code artifact:', error);
      throw error;
    }
```

